      "label": "Independent measurement noise dominates; instruments are functioning but with high noise-to-signal ratio",
      "probability": 0.45,
      "rationale": "The baseline periods show stable means with no detected drift (all four instruments). Cross-correlations between instruments are all within or near chance expectation (pendulum_lab ↔ pendulum_obs: -0.323 vs ±0.374; resonator_lab ↔ resonator_obs: 0.348 vs ±0.529). Autocorrelations at optimal lags are weak and often negative (pendulum_lab: -0.262; resonator_lab: -0.304; resonator_obs: -0.431). This pattern is consistent with white or red noise overwhelming any systematic signal. No physical quantity measured by two independent methods should show near-zero correlation unless measurement error is very large. Today's readings (784763, 24676–584525, 160324–221682, 686963–142635) continue the scatter without obvious anomalies, which supports noise-dominated measurement rather than instrument failure.",
