      "rationale": "Days 1–10 baselines may have been collected under conditions that are not the instrument ground state. If a thermal drift, electromagnetic interference, or calibration offset affected the entire first 10 days, the baseline itself would be a poor reference, and post-baseline drift cannot be detected because we have no post-baseline data yet. The lack of any within-instrument autocorrelation (all weak or negative) would then reflect genuine noise superimposed on a shifted but stable baseline. This hypothesis is compatible with today's readings showing continued scatter. The fact that no instrument shows systematic drift does not rule out this; it only means whatever offset existed was constant during days 1–10.",
