        "No drift detected in any instrument despite 138, 72, 60, and 60 trials respectively (absence of evidence of drift is not evidence of absence of baseline offset)",
        "Weak cross-instrument correlations despite ostensibly measuring related physical quantities"
      ],
      "evidenceAgainst": [
        "Smallest value spacings (0.0001–0.0002) are consistent with instrument resolution; no evidence of quantization artifacts",
        "No level change detected in any stream; a systematic offset would likely manifest as a discontinuity when the instrument returned to normal conditions (which we have not observed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "One or more instruments has a systematic error in readout, data logging, or conversion; readings are internally consistent but decoupled from physical reality or from each other by a constant bias",
